  "articleBody": "It's super easy for a tiny home to feel cluttered if you don't have a plan for all your stuff. But don't worry, there are tons of smart storage solutions out there that can keep your space feeling open and airy. The trick is to think beyond traditional cabinets and really consider how each item in your home can pull double duty. For example, furniture that hides storage inside, like ottomans with lift-up tops or beds with massive under-storage drawers, can be a game-changer. Walls are another underrated asset – floating shelves, wall-mounted racks, and even pegboards can organize items vertically, freeing up precious counter and floor space. Zen Tiny Homes designs with these challenges in mind, creating customized storage that blends right into your home's aesthetic. We've got a decade of experience making tiny homes work, and we've seen it all, from integrated pantry systems to hidden compartments for valuables. The key is to start with a clear idea of what you need to store, then work with designers who know how to weave those needs into the fabric of your home. If clutter is cramping your style, it might be time to explore how a custom tiny home design can solve your storage woes.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-03"
